"skipped": [...]}` → one line in the report: "to the worker queue: N, held: M (reasons)". Nothing is submitted
in this run; the tracker keeps these rows as "🔄 Файли готові", the worker itself moves them to
`portal_submitted`. Do NOT put such jobs into the manual list of the report any more (only `held`, with the reason).

Per the summary JSON update the tracker: `submitted` → status `portal_submitted (портал)` + the path to the confirmation screenshot in Notes; `login_required`/`captcha`/`form_unsupported`/`failed` → leave `ready`, the job goes to the manual list of the report. `login_required` → a separate line in the report: "re-login needed, see docs/server_setup.md". For `interamt` this is the EXPECTED state (the session is server-side and dies with a browser restart): in the report write "Interamt: application ready, a one-time login via VNC is needed, after that the bot does the rest", not as a failure.

